        "source_version": "2024-07-01",
        "source_clause": "§1904.36",
        "source_text_excerpt": "In addition to Sec.1904.35, section 11(c) of the OSH Act also prohibits you from discriminating against an employee for reporting a work-related fatality, injury, or illness. That provision of the Act also protects the employee who files a safety and health complaint, asks for access to the part 1904 records, or otherwise exercises any rights afforded by the OSH Act.",
